WEBVTT

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:09.560
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.450
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.290
but also in crime.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.410
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.130
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.300
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:49.240
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.040
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:01.480
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:07.710
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.260
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:19.560
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.810
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.810
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:32.900
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.900
Just fly fly away

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:42.120
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.840
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:54.180
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:01.350
Save the Terrorists

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.510
<i>Point A3 all clear.</i>

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:37.600
Babylon Project Developer Convention

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.930
Point 4 all clear.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.600
Points 5 and 6 all clear.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.570
I'm so sleepy.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.040
How beautiful!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.290
Will the terrorists try anything?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.090
Hitting the Babylon conference
would really make headlines.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:17.230
With three days of guard duty,
they could have given us a room.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.350
We have a vital duty
to guard and protect!

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.300
Don't fall prey to a lack of sleep!

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.270
It's the cream of the crop,
really extravagant!

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:30.020
It has immense fluffy beds!

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.190
You saw inside?

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.200
Yeah, there's a vacant room.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.230
Pay attention to your duty!

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:42.080
Once we're done today, even
the carrier's tight bed will feel good.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.400
Can I come in for just a minute?

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.670
No!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:06.270
You can hold it. You're not a child!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.400
What's this?

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.860
What are you two doing here?

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.490
Wake up!

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.290
Help!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.420
Hold it right there.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.710
That never seems to work.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.010
Reporting two suspicious men,
possibly with a bomb.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.350
They're fleeing toward
the convention center.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.100
Halt!

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.680
Ohgami, they asked us to halt.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.640
Just shut up and run!

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.430
The bag!

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.010
That was close!

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:34.730
Why are <i>you</i> tired?
I dragged you the whole way!

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.770
Ouch.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.820
This only goes to the observation platform.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.380
We have to think of an escape route.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.790
What's wrong, Yagi?

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.420
You idiot!
What did you do to the switch?

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.620
This is because you threw it!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.880
Do something!

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.470
I can't! Once the count starts,
it detonates in 60 seconds!

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.340
When did it start?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.380
I don't know.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:15.690
Hurry... hurry... hurry!

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.730
What's that sound?

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.980
Fifteen seconds left.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:20.900
Fifteen?

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.880
Is there a problem, sirs?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.120
Get down!

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.840
What?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.090
Well, there it goes.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.880
That was a close one!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.390
We can't get down now.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:07:00.990
It does provide a rather distinctive view.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.250
This will take you to
the east side of the roof.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.280
Then wait for orders.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.790
Understood. Am I clear?

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.880
You're fine.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.030
They saddled us with
a stupid defective bomb!

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:44.230
Of course it went off.
You were too rough with it.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.070
Oh, now you're blaming it on me?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.190
Never mind. What now?
There's no way out.

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:55.250
Without the elevator, we can't get down.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:02.170
Why are you doing that?
You won't get any customers.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:09.970
True, but this is my job.
Bartending is my life.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.440
Labors!

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.790
Hmm, It looks like those two
are acting alone.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:44.000
We've blockaded the road
in front of the hotel.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:49.220
No injuries yet,
but significant structural damage.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.160
The platform could fall.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.270
The whole thing could fall?
That would be bad.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:59.730
Attention suspects. Can you hear me?

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.050
The explosion has damaged
the structural supports.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:10.360
A rescue team is on the way,
so remain calm and follow orders.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.320
The elevator has been blown up,
so you're trapped up there.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:20.240
It's time to abandon your plans
and cooperate. Thank you.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:23.000
Hooray, they're coming to save us!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:29.660
You idiot! They'll save us...
save us for a long prison sentence.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:33.180
No, we'll barricade ourselves here
and halt the Babylon conference!

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.470
Old man, we're taking you hostage!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.850
As you wish.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.330
Aren't you afraid of us?

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:46.110
A bartender
must never leave his counter.

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.030
He's good.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.790
Captain, the lounge looks pretty shaky.
It can't last much longer.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:11.460
Captain, ten different criminal groups
are taking credit.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.010
They must be kidding.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.080
Some people have nothing better to do.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:19.440
Ota, to the right. Noa, cover him.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.640
Roger.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:25.230
It's the Patlabors! Cool!

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:28.740
I'm down to my final resort!

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:32.910
You were carrying that?

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:37.160
The mistake was our dependence on
an electronic timer.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:42.170
Only sweat and sacrifice
will save our precious environment!

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.840
Careful, Ohgami,
that could injure your eyes!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:50.330
Listen up, criminals!
The rescue team is almost there.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:55.260
Follow orders and climb on down.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:00.180
One step closer
and I'll blow you sky high!

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.930
To prove that I'm not bluffing,
I'll light one!

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.690
Be careful!

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:10.440
We don't need your stinking rescue!

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.580
What are they doing?

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.500
I told you so.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:34.840
Noa, grab it!

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.220
<i>How</i>?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.640
<i>Wrap your winch line around the girder!</i>

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.630
<i>Roger.</i>

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:51.440
It's tipping!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.490
It's just your imagination.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.940
See? It stopped.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.120
Stop being stupid and come down.
You're in great danger.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:06.540
Liar! We have a hostage!
<i>You</i> stop being stupid!

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.000
So, an endurance contest.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:14.360
We can wait forever,
but I don't think the supports will last.

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:15.840
Understood.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:22.850
Trouble. There's a fuel pipeline
buried in the road.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.720
That's bad.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.430
Noa, did you copy?

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:32.440
<i>The Labors are close to their limit
but hold on as long as you can.</i>

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.860
Izumi, can you hold it?

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.450
I don't know.

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:52.050
But if this falls,
it'll be a massive disaster.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.940
<i>This is the Home of the Sea,
Tokyo branch the "Caged Birds!"</i>

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.120
<i>Our codenames are
"Nightingale" and "Ebony Dodo."</i>

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:27.790
The Babylon Project must be halted!
Save the planet!

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:32.000
You selfish city dwellers
need to think of future generations!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:38.250
Stop wasting toilet paper, and, and...

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.580
What should I say now?

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:40.550
I don't know.

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.420
His speech is only half-finished.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.350
They're a wily and unpredictable foe.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:55.980
Captain, the Ingrams can't hold for long.
They need help fast!

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:58.990
Captain, we're on the road
in front of the hotel.

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:03.910
The fuel pipeline looks pretty vulnerable.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:09.040
And the airport says
that even if they stop the fuel,

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.680
they can't drain the pipeline.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.250
I guess I have no choice.

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.290
Where are you going?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.590
I'll be back soon.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:24.800
I only came 'cause you said
we'd dump the bomb in a trashcan!

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.560
That's what I planned!

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:31.240
But we hid, fell asleep,
and then set off the bomb.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.950
We're serious felons now.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.160
A little late for complaints.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:40.610
Messing up their conference
would have been good enough.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:45.530
Of course!

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.790
While we're here,
they can't hold the conference!

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.570
We won't give up!

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:51.820
But...

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:56.420
Yeah, they're in big trouble.
First, we'll demand food.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:58.960
Oh, would you like something to eat?

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.170
What?

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.220
I can provide anything
from our morning menu.

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:09.810
I demand one club sandwich!

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.020
Me too!

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:15.520
Very good. Would you like
onion and tomato with that?

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:21.690
How long do we have to do this?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.460
<i>Ota, do you read</i>?

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.980
Yes, sir.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.480
Can you talk to the terrorists?

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.910
<i>Me, sir?</i>

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:33.070
I'm a little busy right now. Thanks.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.660
Yes, sir!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.960
Listen up, lawbreakers!

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:42.040
It's dangerous in there,
so you better come out right now!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.710
Liar!

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:44.760
What?

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:45.920
We'll come out

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:50.720
If you guarantee our safety
and halt the Babylon conference.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:55.140
You have the nerve to make demands?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:59.100
Watch your mouth! We have a hostage.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.520
What?

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.910
<i>That's correct. A bartender
named Maki was setting up.</i>

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.910
<i>Take care of that, too, won't you</i>?

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.440
Damn!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:13.400
Do as we say,
or our hostage will pay the price!

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:17.080
Then I'll see
that <i>you</i> pay the price, too!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:21.000
Is a policeman
supposed to talk to us like that?

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:24.670
Don't think you're going
to get away with this!

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:29.050
Oh yeah?
I'd like to see you <i>try</i> to save us!

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:32.470
The only message
I have for you is this!

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.310
Ota, no!

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.360
What are you doing, Ota?

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:58.700
<i>Officer Ota, have you forgotten
about the hostage</i>?

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.790
<i>Ota, didn't you hear
about the pipeline</i>?

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.510
<i>Ota, what's going on</i>?

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:08.300
Damn! Why do I have to
save these jerks?

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.910
I wish I'd never helped you!

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:17.230
Fine! Just go home then!

00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:22.860
This is why you don't have any friends!

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:29.820
You looked lonely,
after being turned down by every group.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.030
I just wanted to help.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.910
We aren't part of
the Home of the Sea,

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.910
it was all your idea!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.670
And those stupid codenames!

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:42.810
I wanted to be a hawk or an eagle,
not the "Ebony Dodo."

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.550
It's too hard to be your friend!

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:46.670
Listen...

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:51.140
All right, all right. I'm sorry.
It's all my fault.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.300
Try this.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.740
Thank you.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.060
Here.

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:05.320
Too strong?

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:07.400
What was it?

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:14.300
A boilermaker. Whiskey with
a beer chaser. A real pick-me-up.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:15.560
One more.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:17.330
Coming right up, sir.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.160
<i>Don't tell Ota.</i>

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.740
Why not?

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:24.930
I'm not sure how he'd react.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:29.420
It's a little risky, but it's
our best plan for minimizing damage.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.570
Can you do it?

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:31.840
I'll do my best.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.010
Then I leave it in your hands.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.180
Roger.

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:49.640
What are you doing?

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:53.110
Maybe we should try to talk them out.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:58.070
You're suggesting we give in
and beg them to come out?

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:01.510
I thought you might
be able to persuade them.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:04.250
Really? You think it's okay?

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.130
At the scene,
you have to use your judgment.

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.960
All right!

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.340
Hey criminal scum! Come out <i>now!</i>

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:19.470
You again? Are you losers still here?

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.930
<i>Don't underestimate us!</i>

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:28.900
We're professional terrorists!

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.280
Are you mocking Division 2?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:36.910
I've had all I can stand!

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:42.000
He's going to kill us! He's a lunatic!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:46.750
Say your prayers, villains!
This'll only take one shot!

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.310
Lucky idiots!

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.020
Detonate.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:14.360
What's going on?

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:39.970
I'd like to call this a success.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:43.900
At least we didn't break
the fuel pipe.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:46.390
Where are the hostage and criminals?

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:49.150
Izumi should have rescued them.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:52.640
Should have? And where's Officer Ota?

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:56.020
He's in his Ingram. He should be okay.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.860
Sh-Should be?

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.700
<i>Noa, are you all right? Noa!</i>

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.930
I'm fine.

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:16.260
Mr. Maki, isn't it? Are you all right?

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:22.380
Yes, but how bold, destroying
the bar to save everything else!

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.340
I'm sorry, our captain
can be a bit heavy-handed.

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:28.430
No, it takes great subtlety to be bold.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:33.680
Your captain
would make a fine bartender!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.940
A bartender?

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.780
Where's Ota?

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.120
Still alive.

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:42.400
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:45.540
Izumi, did you know
about the explosion?

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:47.970
Well...

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:52.700
<i>Captain, why didn't you tell me</i>?

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:56.510
<i>Captain, answer me!</i>

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:02.030
He deserves an answer, Captain Goto.

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:04.390
I've been so patient...

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:07.350
I have to tinkle!

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:13.270
Take care of this for me!

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:20.520
<i>Captain, why haven't you answered?
Don't you trust me</i>?

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:25.110
<i>Ota, Noa's the only one he told.
We were surprised, too</i>.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:29.070
<i>That's right, Ota. I was the only one.</i>

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:32.240
<i>I don't think he wanted
to burden us with the knowledge.</i>

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:40.720
<i>Shut up, I'm talking to the captain.
Captain, answer me!</i>

00:22:59.940 --> 00:23:04.450
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:12.210
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:14.170
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:19.630
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:28.190
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:29.890
I got it

00:23:29.890 --> 00:23:37.430
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:43.310
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:44.860
One more chance

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:52.490
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:58.430
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:58.430 --> 00:24:01.920
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:11.430
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:11.430
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:18.350
So, some of them are <i>at</i> the airport,
and some of them are <i>in</i> the airport?

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:22.360
Yes, they are wanted men.

00:24:22.360 --> 00:24:25.230
Inubashiri has the skills,
Nekowatari has the heart,

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:28.270
and Sankichi Sarusuberi has the brains.

00:24:28.270 --> 00:24:30.230
Dog, cat, and monkey...
What is this, a zoo?

00:24:30.230 --> 00:24:32.360
When these three get together,
who knows what they're gonna do!

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:34.570
If we knew the answer to that,
this would be easy.

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:38.830
Next episode: The Men Who Returned.
Target, locked on!

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:43.330
Next episode

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:43.330
The Men Who Returned
